.TH BTRFS\-GAME\-COMPRESSOR 1 "2026" "btrfs-game-compressor 0.3.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
btrfs\-game\-compressor \- compress Steam game libraries on Btrfs with ZSTD
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B btrfs\-game\-compressor
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B btrfs\-game\-compressor
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B btrfs\-game\-compressor
discovers Steam game libraries that live on a Btrfs filesystem and compresses
their contents with one ZSTD pass.
The bundled bgc-native executable performs compression and deduplication through
Linux kernel interfaces. No external filesystem utilities are required.
Deduplication scans each selected game after compression; explicit library passes
can share data between games. Logical file contents and names are preserved.
Already-compressed archives, video, and audio may gain little from another
compression pass. Filesystem compression keeps game file contents unchanged;
actual savings and runtime effects vary by game and device.
.PP
Run with no arguments it starts an interactive terminal UI. The
.BR \-\-status ", " \-\-dry\-run " and " \-\-library
modes are non\-interactive, change nothing unexpected, and are safe to pipe or
run from a script.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-status
Print a non\-interactive report of every discovered game and its state, then
exit. Requires no terminal.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
List the games that a batch compression would process, without modifying
anything.
.TP
.B \-\-dedupe
Run the native backend over each discovered Btrfs Steam library, including games already
marked compressed. A library is skipped while one of its games is running. The
report measures unique file-data extent bytes before and after, and shows how
much the physical game-data footprint decreased. Root permission is needed for this
measurement; without it, deduplication still runs and the saved amount is shown
as unavailable.
.TP
.B \-\-recheck
Remeasure every discovered game and refresh its current original and on-disk sizes without recompressing files. Existing compression timestamps are preserved, so changed games remain marked updated. Requires root permission for Btrfs extent measurements.
.TP
.BI \-\-assets " GAME"
Preview beta asset optimization for one installed game at the configured
profile. Supported media include loose images, simple legacy DDS textures, and
simple mono/stereo PCM or 32-bit-float WAV. Non-native profiles emit integer
PCM. GAME is an exact name or full install path.
.TP
.B \-\-assets\-all
Fast read\-only extension/format inventory for every installed game. Reports
candidate containers and understood formats without decoding and changes
nothing.
.TP
.B \-\-assets\-verify\-all
Read\-only Balanced transform\-candidate scan for every installed game. It
decodes candidates to estimate logical reductions but writes nothing. Engine
asset rewriting is beta; an empty candidate row is a coverage gap, not a
failure.
.TP
.B \-\-compact\-all\-no\-backup
Checkpointed library pass: apply supported Balanced assets, then Zstd
compression, then dedupe, for every installed game. Python 3 is required.
This is \fBirreversible\fR: no asset restore copy is retained, and an
interrupted asset stage is flagged for manual recovery rather than repeated;
recover original assets with Steam verification. Running games and games with
existing recovery data are skipped. Results and a savings chart are written
under \fI$XDG_STATE_HOME/btrfs\-game\-compressor/compact\-balanced\fR. Unsupported
formats are left byte\-for\-byte untouched, and completion is not full asset
coverage or proof of in\-game compatibility. Exits nonzero if any game fails or
is skipped.
.TP
.BI \-\-export\-fmod " QUALITY FILE OUTPUT"
Experimental native lossy FMOD Vorbis export (quality 0.0 through 0.4).
Named profiles conservative and balanced use quality 0.3 and 0.2, require 5%
stream savings including seek metadata, and reject candidates below a sparse
decoded-waveform SNR guard of 20 dB and 18 dB. Numeric quality uses 15 dB.
These offline checks are not a perceptual-quality guarantee.
Rebuild supported FSB5 v1 or single-FSB RIFF/FEV banks into a new, smaller file.
The source and existing output files are never overwritten. Playback rates,
declared durations and non-codec metadata are preserved; packet offsets and
seek tables are rebuilt. Not enabled for automatic game-asset replacement;
in-game audio, loop and seeking validation is required. Bink 2 re-encoding is
not implemented.
.TP
.BI \-\-texture\-compress " MAX_DIM FILE OUTPUT"
Export\-only DDS downscale (experimental). Decodes the base mip of a bounded 2D
DDS texture, downscales it to MAX_DIM without upscaling, re\-encodes it to the
same codec with a regenerated mip chain, and writes OUTPUT. The source is never
modified and an existing OUTPUT is refused. Supported inputs are legacy
BC1/BC2/BC3 and 32\-bit BGRA/RGBA, plus DX10 BC1/BC2/BC3/BC4/BC5/BC7 and
R8G8B8A8/B8G8R8A8; cubemaps, arrays, volumes, BC6H and float formats are
rejected. The exported payload is lossy, the container is verified by
re\-parsing and re\-decoding, and the result is not validated in\-game and is not
applied to installed games.
.TP
.BI \-\-texture\-compress\-tree " MAX_DIM DIR OUTPUT_DIR"
Export\-only pass over a directory tree. Mirrors every `.dds` under DIR into
OUTPUT_DIR at the same relative path, downscaling each to MAX_DIM with the same
codec and a rebuilt mip chain, and writes only files that actually shrink. DIR is
never modified; unsupported or existing files are skipped and reported. Like
\-\-texture\-compress, the payloads are lossy, unverified in\-game, and never
applied to installed games.
.TP
.BI \-\-apply\-assets " GAME"
Apply beta asset optimization to a stopped game, retaining originals in a
local restore copy. Visual media may lose detail; supported WAV files may be
resampled, and Ultra Performance may reduce PCM to 8-bit with deterministic
dither. Resized 8-bit RGB/RGBA images may be quantized (alpha is retained).
Higher audio tiers target up to 16-bit PCM without up-converting. Hades v7 LZ4
packages can be recompressed losslessly, preserving decoded assets and manifests.
The Lossless profile only enables this package
pass. Bink, FMOD and other packed formats are not re-encoded. Requires terminal
confirmation. Opus conversion is not attempted because game compatibility
depends on the expected codec and container.
The Lossless workflow requires a fresh backup set and exact privileged Btrfs
measurements. It attempts to restore individual packages that fail physical
storage comparisons, and restores the entire new pass if the aggregate live
footprint is not strictly smaller or the post-apply measurement fails. Logical
package reductions alone are not sufficient. Backups still consume storage
until explicitly finalized; snapshots can retain their blocks afterwards.
.TP
.BI \-\-engines " GAME"
Read-only report of the game engine (Unity, Unreal, Godot, RE Engine,
GameMaker, ...) and of its largest containers classified by kind
(\fIunity-stream\fR, \fIunity-bundle\fR, \fIpak\fR, \fIunreal-iostore\fR,
\fIgodot-pck\fR, \fIfmod-audio\fR, \fIwwise-audio\fR, \fIbink-video\fR). It
changes nothing and needs no privilege, and reports engines it does not
recognize honestly.
.TP
.BI \-\-audit\-container " FILE"
Read-only, content-detected UnityFS compression analysis, standalone Unity
SerializedFile v17-22 metadata/class inventory, Godot PCK resource inventory, or
Unreal Pak footer and bounded unencrypted primary-index SHA1 inspection.
Supported Unity type trees expose bounded texture fields without resolving stream
paths. Unencrypted Pak v1-9 directory/data headers and v10/v11 path-hash and
directory-index SHA1 values are checked before bounded entry classification.
Modern/compressed/encrypted payloads and signatures remain
unverified. IoStore TOC v1-8 headers expose counts, security/partition metadata,
minimum file-size bounds and regular companion presence only; chunk arrays,
signatures and .ucas payloads remain unverified.
No Unity/Unreal texture or audio writer is enabled.
Reports logical sizes, not physical
savings. Unsupported codecs, encryption and layouts are not bypassed.
.TP
.BI \-\-export\-unityfs " FILE OUTPUT"
Experimental lossless UnityFS v6-8 LZ4/HC recompression to a new file. Keeps
decoded bytes and block boundaries; does not resize textures. Maximum input
512 MiB. Stored blocks and codec flags remain unchanged. Catalog/hash and game
compatibility require separate validation; no installed auto-apply.
.TP
.BI \-\-export\-godot " FILE OUTPUT"
Experimental lossless standalone plain Godot PCK v1-4 resource deduplication to a new
file. Identical payloads share offsets, after byte-for-byte comparison; all
exported resources are verified. Rejects encrypted/sparse/unknown layouts.
Both container export modes refuse existing destinations and require logical
savings divided by complete output bytes to meet min_gain_pct before writing.
The source remains unchanged, so an export is not net storage savings.
.TP
.BI \-\-audit\-godot\-textures " PROFILE FILE"
Read-only estimate of how much a Godot PCK would shrink if supported
.B .stex / .ctex
textures were downscaled and RGB-quantized for the selected profile. Writes nothing.
.TP
.BI \-\-audit\-godot3\-audio " PROFILE FILE"
Read-only estimate of how much a Godot 3 PCK v1 would shrink if its
.B AudioStreamMP3
resources were re-encoded as Ogg Vorbis. Writes nothing.
.TP
.BI \-\-export\-godot3\-audio " PROFILE FILE OUTPUT"
Experimental, lossy, export-only Godot 3 PCK audio rewrite. Each
.B AudioStreamMP3
resource is decoded and re-encoded as Ogg Vorbis under the same entry name, and
the matching
.B .import
stub's
.B type=
is switched to
.B AudioStreamOGGVorbis
(Godot 3 loads a resource by its stored type, not its extension). Supported PCM
samples are also reduced in rate/bit depth with scaled loop points; IMA-ADPCM
is disabled. Other entries are copied byte-for-byte and byte-compared. Refuses existing destinations, uses
the same min_gain_pct output-write gate, never overwrites the installed pack, and
is not auto-applied. Brotato passed manual playtesting; other games require
independent playback/loop checks. Godot 4 audio is not covered.
.TP
.BI \-\-export\-godot\-textures " PROFILE FILE OUTPUT"
Experimental, lossy, export-only Godot PCK texture rewrite. Supported
.B .stex / .ctex
(Godot 3 GDST / Godot 4 GST2) textures -- supported WebP/PNG and block formats
BC1/BC2/BC3/BC7 -- are downscaled and RGB-quantized for the selected profile.
Logical dimensions and codecs are preserved and resized mip chains are rebuilt.
Unsupported encodings are copied byte-for-byte; non-shrinking changes are discarded.
The pack is rebuilt with relocated offsets and recomputed MD5 and
re-parsed; untouched entries are byte-compared. Refuses existing destinations,
uses the same min_gain_pct output-write gate, never overwrites the installed
pack, and is not auto-applied. Brotato passed manual playtesting; Godot 4
requires per-game tests. Native/Lossless makes no changes.
.TP
.BI \-\-slim " GAME"
One offline, reversible pass that keeps the highest resolution tier and the
host-platform build, removing other resolution fallbacks and non-host platform
folders plus debug symbols. With a language list set it also removes every
language pack you did not select (localized audio, subtitles and locale data); a
group is skipped unless one of your languages is present, so no language set is
ever emptied. Format-agnostic (directory shape and names only) and
has no runtime component. Everything is written to the restorable backup tree;
confirm with \-\-restore\-assets or free space with \-\-finalize\-assets. Groups
it cannot classify unambiguously are left untouched. Requires terminal
confirmation.
.TP
.BI \-\-keep\-languages " LIST"
Set the languages \-\-slim keeps, as codes or English names separated by commas
(for example en,de or English,German). Stored in the keep_languages settings
file. An empty list disables language pruning. Keep the language the game boots
with; removing it can prevent startup, and every removal stays restorable.
.TP
.BI \-\-variants " GAME"
Read-only, format-agnostic report of sibling suites that share an identical
file-name layout but differ in data: architecture builds, renderer or shader
suites, resolution tiers, platform folders and language packs. Groups whose
members do not look like variants (sequential level, region or skin folders)
are suppressed. Shows the bytes reclaimable by keeping one member; changes
nothing and needs no privilege.
.TP
.BI \-\-prune\-assets " GAME"
Move developer debug symbols (*.pdb, *.ilk) that a released build does not load
into the restorable backup tree, then remove them from the game. Only regular
files are selected; symlinks and escaping paths are rejected. Recover with
\-\-restore\-assets; free space returns after \-\-finalize\-assets. Requires
terminal confirmation.
.TP
.BI \-\-prune\-fallbacks " GAME"
As \-\-prune\-assets, and additionally remove low-resolution (720p) and BC3
texture/video fallback suites. The engine loads those only when it selects
low-resolution assets (for example on a weak GPU or by explicit setting).
Use only when this machine renders the full-resolution assets; otherwise the
game can fail to find them. Fully restorable.
.TP
.BI \-\-restore\-assets " GAME"
Restore original files from the local restore copy.
.TP
.BI \-\-finalize\-assets " GAME"
Discard the local restore copy after testing the game. Requires a terminal
confirmation. Steam verification may be needed to recover the original files.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
List each file while compressing or deduplicating. By default, only periodic
progress and final space measurements are printed.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " "\-\-library " \fIDIR\fR
Register \fIDIR\fR as an extra game library and exit. Accepts either the library
root or its \fBsteamapps/common\fR subdirectory. A warning is printed if the path
is not on a Btrfs filesystem.
.TP
.B \-\-pending
With \fB\-\-status\fR or \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR, restrict output to games that are not
yet compressed.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable ANSI color output. The \fBNO_COLOR\fR environment variable has the same
effect.
.TP
.B \-\-json
With \fB\-\-status\fR or \fB\-\-ratios\fR, emit a JSON object (for \fB\-\-status\fR,
the discovered libraries, game records, and a summary; for \fB\-\-ratios\fR, the
table entries). This option requires \fB\-\-status\fR, \fB\-\-benchmark\fR or
\fB\-\-ratios\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-history
Print separate ZSTD compression and deduplication histories, newest first.
Deduplication rows show physical data extents before and after and the measured
shared bytes. This reads the history files and changes nothing.
.TP
.B \-\-stats
Print ZSTD compression savings and the latest measured dedupe estimate for each
library. The dedupe figure sums only each library's newest measured pass, not all
historical passes. Reads the history files and changes nothing.
.TP
.B \-\-benchmark
Print the measured saving for each game, sorted from best to worst, followed by a
summary: total size before and after, the overall ratio, the best single game,
and how many games save more than 50%. Every figure is derived from recorded
Btrfs extent measurements, so it describes real disks rather than an estimate. With
.BR \-\-json ,
the same data is emitted as JSON.
.TP
.B \-\-ratios \fR[\fIGAME\fR]
Look up expected savings in the community table maintained in
\fIratios/games.json\fR. With no argument the whole table is printed; with a game
name, only that game's rows. Every row names the zstd level it was measured at,
because a game's ratio is a property of \fI(game, level)\fR and a level\-1
measurement must not be applied to a \fBzstd:6\fR library. The table is a hint
only: a local \fB\-\-benchmark\fR measurement always wins, and none of the ratio
modes ever compresses anything. The table is installed with the tool, so
\fB\-\-ratios\fR works without a network connection or a git checkout. A
first\-pass game the table expects to save under \fBmin_gain_pct\fR is flagged
\fBlikely low yield\fR in \fB\-\-status\fR and \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR, as an advisory
only: it is still listed and still compressed, because only a local pass can
measure it. With \fB\-\-json\fR the entries are emitted as JSON.
.TP
.B \-\-export\-ratios
Emit this machine's measured savings as a valid ratios document, ready to merge
into \fIratios/games.json\fR and submit as a pull request. Repeated measurements
of the same game at the same level are averaged into one row that also records
the sample count and the min/max range. Nothing is uploaded; the output goes to
standard output.
.TP
.B \-\-import\-ratios \fIFILE\fR
Read \fIFILE\fR as a community ratios document and use it as a fallback hint for
games this machine has not measured. The file is cached at
\fI~/.config/btrfs\-game\-compressor/ratios_hint.json\fR. A file that parses to no
entries is rejected, so a bad merge can never be cached as if it were a table.
.TP
.B \-\-render\-ratios
Render the community table as a Markdown document on standard output. This is the
maintainer command behind \fImake ratios\-doc\fR, which regenerates
\fIGAMES.md\fR. It always reads the shipped \fIratios/games.json\fR and ignores
any table imported with \fB\-\-import\-ratios\fR, so a maintainer's personal
measurements can never leak into the committed document. It needs no tooling
beyond the script itself.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-update
Ask the release API whether a newer version exists and print the answer. This is
read-only and changes nothing.
.TP
.B \-\-self\-update
Download the latest release and install it over the running script, verifying the
archive against the release's \fISHA256SUMS\fR first. It refuses when the script
is owned by a package manager (a distro package under \fI/usr\fR, Homebrew, or
Nix) and tells you to update through it instead, and it leaves the running copy
untouched if the checksum does
not match. The update takes effect on the next run. A newer release is also looked
for automatically at most once a day (disable with the \fIauto_update\fR config
file), or whenever the watch timer runs \fB\-\-notify\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-uninstall
Remove the tool, its manpage, the community ratio table installed beside it, and
the optional systemd user units. It asks for confirmation at a terminal, refuses
when the script is owned by a package manager, and never deletes the user's
configuration or compression history.
.TP
.B \-\-submit\-ratios
Offer this machine's measured savings back to the project by opening a GitHub
issue containing the same document \fB\-\-export\-ratios\fR emits: game names, the
zstd level, the saving, and the sample count and range. No paths, host details or
other personal data are included, nothing is sent without confirmation, and it
requires the optional \fBgh\fR command from the GitHub CLI, logged in as the user.
A maintainer merges the submission, so the shared table cannot be poisoned by an
unreviewed client.
.TP
.B \-\-yes
With \fB\-\-uninstall\fR or \fB\-\-submit\-ratios\fR, skip the confirmation prompt.
It does not override the package\-manager refusal.
.TP
.B \-\-notify
Send a desktop notification for games in COMPRESSED, UPDATED or UNCOMPRESSED state when compression or deduplication is pending.
This is read-only and does not start compression. Requires the optional
\fBnotify-send\fR command from libnotify.
.TP
.B \-\-balance
Offer a native metadata balance for each Btrfs mount holding a discovered library.
This is a privileged, whole-filesystem operation and is not needed to reclaim
space from deduplication. It is never implied by status or dry-run commands.
The tool prints the native command and requires interactive confirmation.
.SH INTERACTIVE KEYS
.TP
.BR "↑" ", " ↓ ", " k ", " j
Move the cursor.
.TP
.BR "←" ", " → ", " h ", " l
Previous or next page.
.TP
.B Space
Toggle the checkbox on the highlighted game.
.TP
.B a
Toggle every game on the current page.
.TP
.BR Enter ", " c
Compress the highlighted game, or every checked game.
.TP
.B b
Batch\-compress everything still pending.
.TP
.B o
Preview the configured [BETA] asset profile for the highlighted game and optionally
apply it after confirmation.
.TP
.B f
Search and filter the list.
.TP
.B v
Show only games that still need compressing.
.TP
.B t
Show compression statistics.
.TP
.B s
Open settings: speed/throttle mode and library management.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SH GAME STATES
.TP
.B COMPRESSED
Compression is current, but no successful dedupe pass is recorded since it. Batch mode deduplicates this game without recompressing it.
.TP
.B COMPACTED
Compressed and deduplicated, with no later file changes.
.TP
.B UNCOMPRESSED
Never compressed by this tool.
.TP
.B RUNNING
A live process has a file open under the game's install directory, so the game
is in use. It is held back, and re\-checked immediately before any write, so a
game started during a batch is not rewritten underneath itself. Running games
are also counted separately by
.BR \-\-status .
.PP
Change detection is a recursive
.B find \-newermt
over the entire game directory, so updates deep inside a game's data tree are
still detected. \fBProton*\fR, \fBSteamLinuxRuntime*\fR and the Steam shared
folders are skipped automatically.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/btrfs\-game\-compressor/custom_libraries.txt
Extra library roots, one per line.
.TP
.I ~/.config/btrfs\-game\-compressor/throttle.conf
\fB0\fR for full speed, \fB1\fR to wrap defragmentation in
.BR "nice \-n 19 ionice \-c 2 \-n 7" .
.TP
.I ~/.config/btrfs\-game\-compressor/min_size_mib
Installs holding less than this many MiB of file data are treated as empty
download leftovers and skipped. \fB0\fR disables the filter.
.TP
.I ~/.config/btrfs\-game\-compressor/compress_level
Zstd level passed to
.BR "btrfs filesystem defragment \-L" .
\fBauto\fR, the default, mirrors the level the library's mount point is configured
with so that the library stays uniformly compressed; a value of \fB1\fR to \fB15\fR
pins a level instead. \fBcompress\-force=\fR takes precedence over \fBcompress=\fR
when a mount specifies both.
.TP
.I ~/.config/btrfs\-game\-compressor/min_gain_pct
An updated game whose previous saving was less than this percentage of its size is
reported as \fBLOW YIELD\fR and held back. Because both the cost of a
defragmentation pass and its benefit scale with the size of the game, the
percentage is the meaningful test: it does not matter whether a game is 100 MB or
100 GB, only how well it compresses. \fB0\fR disables the test. Default \fB5\fR.
.TP
.I ~/.config/btrfs\-game\-compressor/min_prune_mib
The minimum saving for a delete-only prune (\-\-slim, \-\-prune\-assets) to be
offered. Deleting writes almost nothing, so it is judged by this small absolute
floor rather than by the ratio that governs compression. \fB0\fR disables it.
Default \fB1\fR.
.TP
.I ~/.config/btrfs\-game\-compressor/auto_update
\fB1\fR (the default) lets the tool look for a newer release at most once a day;
\fB0\fR disables the automatic check. \fB\-\-check\-update\fR and
\fB\-\-self\-update\fR work regardless.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/btrfs\-game\-compressor/compressed_games.db
Compression measurements, original logical file sizes and compression timestamps. The recorded
sizes are what the \fBLOW YIELD\fR predictions are derived from, so a game is never
judged before it has been compressed at least once. Records are keyed by escaped
install path; legacy name-keyed records are ignored during the one-time migration.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/btrfs\-game\-compressor/dedupe_completed.db
Successful dedupe pass timestamps used to distinguish COMPRESSED from COMPACTED.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/btrfs\-game\-compressor/dedupe/
Temporary native sort files, progress logs and per-library locks. Each pass
rehashes its selected scope. Temporary files are cleaned up on normal exit and
handled signals; forced termination may leave a native-* scratch directory.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/btrfs\-game\-compressor/dedupe_physical_history.db
Append-only before/after measurements for successful dedupe passes. These are kept
separate from the ZSTD compression history and are shown by \fB\-\-history\fR and
\fB\-\-stats\fR.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Bash 4+, the bundled static bgc-native executable, awk, coreutils, findutils and
util-linux (including flock). The backend supports x86_64 and aarch64 Linux.
Explicit ZSTD compression levels require Linux 6.15 or later.
No btrfs-progs, compsize or duperemove package is required. Root permission is
needed to read compressed extent metadata and to balance a filesystem.
Without measurement permission, savings are reported as n/a.
.B notify\-send
from libnotify is optional and is needed only for \fB\-\-notify\fR.
.PP
The library's filesystem must be Btrfs and mounted with a \fBcompress=\fR or
\fBcompress\-force=\fR option, otherwise new extents inherit no compression:
.PP
.RS
.nf
UUID=xxxx  /mnt/games  btrfs  compress=zstd,noatree  0  0
.fi
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
A required command is missing, a path given to \fB\-\-library\fR does not exist,
or interactive mode was requested without a terminal.
.TP
.B 2
The command line could not be parsed.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.nf
btrfs\-game\-compressor
btrfs\-game\-compressor \-\-status
btrfs\-game\-compressor \-\-status \-\-pending
btrfs\-game\-compressor \-\-dry\-run
btrfs\-game\-compressor \-\-dedupe
btrfs\-game\-compressor \-\-library /mnt/games
btrfs\-game\-compressor \-\-status \-\-no\-color | column \-t
btrfs\-game\-compressor \-\-status \-\-json
btrfs\-game\-compressor \-\-stats
btrfs\-game\-compressor \-\-history
btrfs\-game\-compressor \-\-benchmark
btrfs\-game\-compressor \-\-ratios
btrfs\-game\-compressor \-\-ratios "Factorio"
btrfs\-game\-compressor \-\-export\-ratios
btrfs\-game\-compressor \-\-notify
btrfs\-game\-compressor \-\-balance
btrfs\-game\-compressor \-\-compact\-all\-no\-backup
btrfs\-game\-compressor \-\-texture\-compress 1920 texture.dds out/texture.dds
btrfs\-game\-compressor \-\-texture\-compress\-tree 1920 assets/ out/assets/
.fi
